  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "zlovzab95q5g",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "acggiqxmmtkq"
              ],
              "text": "Farafra Oasis"
            },
            {
              "_key": "9s1muzurba1r",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ": Echoes of the Past"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "acggiqxmmtkq",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58849",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The Farafra Oasis, a jewel in Egypt’s Western Desert, holds tales as ancient and mysterious as the sands surrounding it. Known as Ta-iht in antiquity, its mention in Pharaonic texts, such as the Dynasty V official’s titulary and the story of ‘The Eloquent Peasant’ from King Khety’s reign, stirs intrigue. This enigmatic oasis was once acknowledged in the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Luxor Temple"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " as a source of dates and minerals during Rameses II’s era, with further references to its occupation by Libyan troops in Merenptah’s reign, as noted in the Karnak Temple inscription."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/luxor-travel-guide/the-luxor-temple/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/luxor/the-luxor-temple",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "A Place of Legends and Myths"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000013",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Farafra, the third among the Seven Oases as recorded in the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000a"
              ],
              "text": "Edfu Temple"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", is enveloped in legends that transcend its sparse archaeological footprint. One such legend ties Farafra to the enigmatic vanishing of Persian King "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000d"
              ],
              "text": "Cambyses’"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " army. As narrated by Herodotus, this 50,000-strong force vanished without a trace in a sandstorm en route from Thebes to "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000010"
              ],
              "text": "Siwa"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", fueling centuries of fascination and exploration."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Edfu",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/cambyses-opers",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/siwa-oasis-travel-guide/historical-tapestry/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/siwa-oasis-travel-guide/historical-tapestry/",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000015",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Roman Footprints and Medieval Majesty"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The few archaeological sites in Farafra predominantly date back to the Roman Period. The region once hosted a fortress, a sentinel along ancient caravan routes. Most Roman ruins cluster around Qasr el-Farafra, the oasis’s current capital, which was historically its sole village. The "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000017"
              ],
              "text": "Qasr"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", a fortress overlooking the desert, likely stands on a Roman foundation, expanded in Medieval times with over 125 rooms. Despite damage from 1950s rain, it remains a partly inhabited symbol of resilience."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/bahariya-oasis-travel-guide/al-qasr-village/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/bahariya-oasis/al-qasr-village",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Buried Secrets and Christian Hermitage "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000021",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Nearby lies an ancient cemetery, where rock-cut tombs, some later homes to early Christian hermits, are "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000001e"
              ],
              "text": "nearly swallowed by the desert"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". Ahmed Fakhry, a revered Egyptian archaeologist, highlighted Ain Besai, about 12km from Qasr el-Farafra, as a site of significance, featuring a Roman cemetery and a limestone chapel among its treasures."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/sharm-el-sheikh-airport-transfer/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/sharm-el-sheikh-airport-transfer",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000023",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The Allure of the White Desert"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000024",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Farafra is now famed for the breathtaking White Desert to its north-east, a protected area of surreal landscapes. Safari "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000026",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000025"
              ],
              "text": "explorers"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000027",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " here often visit Ain Hadra, a Roman-Byzantine era spring, where palm trees and ancient pottery sherds tell tales of a time long passed. The spring is part of the picturesque Ain el-Wadi, once a Roman habitation site, its fields now relics of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000029",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000028"
              ],
              "text": "history"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000025",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/nuweiba-travel-guide/exploring/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/nuweiba-travel-guide/exploring/",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000028",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/the-worlds-first-labour-strike/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/blog/kiroku-ni-nokoru-saiko-kyu-no-rodo-sutoraiki",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Traces of Ancient Civilizations"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Venturing further, Wadi Abu Hannis unveils remnants of Roman mudbrick structures, and 70km north, the Hidden Valley, or Wadi el-Obeid, reveals prehistoric traces. An Italian-Egyptian mission has unearthed evidence of a Neolithic village from the 8th millennium BC, offering a glimpse into the lives of the Libyan Desert’s earliest pastoral inhabitants."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Farafra-Oasis-1.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "A lone hiker traversing the sculpted dunes and rock formations of a desert landscape with patches of snow."
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "Contrasts of Nature: A lone explorer's journey through Farafra's sandy vastness, where the desert's heat clings to the cold touch of winter's snow"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000031",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/a04ef119a35e506f8ead.jpeg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "An adobe-style mud-brick fort with ornate carvings and palm trees against a bright blue sky"
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "Ancient artistry meets desert architecture in this mud-brick fortification, standing as a testament to enduring craftsmanship"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "es",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "zt4flaue3m9i",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Resumen Histórico De Oasis De "
            },
            {
              "_key": "s9urx5qyhyfo",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "kxzv7skp6qv2"
              ],
              "text": "Farafra"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "kxzv7skp6qv2",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58849",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "El oasis de Farafra, una joya del desierto occidental de Egipto, encierra historias tan antiguas y misteriosas como las arenas que lo rodean."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Conocido como Ta-iht en la antigüedad, su mención en textos faraónicos, como el titulario del funcionario de la Dinastía V y la historia de «El campesino elocuente» del reinado del rey Khety, despierta la intriga."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Este enigmático oasis fue reconocido en su día en "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000007"
              ],
              "text": "el Templo de Luxor"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " como fuente de dátiles y minerales durante la época de Ramsés II, con otras referencias a su ocupación por tropas libias en el reinado de Merenptah, como se señala en la inscripción del Templo de Karnak. "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-luxor/el-templo-de-luxor/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/luxor/el-templo-de-luxor",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Un lugar de leyendas y mitos"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Farafra, el tercero de los Siete Oasis según consta en el Templo de "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000000e"
              ],
              "text": "Edfu"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", está envuelto en leyendas que trascienden su escasa huella arqueológica."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Una de esas leyendas vincula a Farafra con la enigmática desaparición del ejército del rey persa "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000013"
              ],
              "text": "Cambises"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Según narra Heródoto, esta fuerza "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000018"
              ],
              "text": "de 50.000 hombres desapareció sin dejar rastro en una tormenta de arena cuando se dirigía de Tebas a Siwa"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", lo que alimentó siglos de fascinación y exploración."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-de-edfu/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/edfu",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://es.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cambises",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/oasis-de-siwa-una-aventura-epica-eterna/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/blog/oasis-de-siwa-una-aventura-epica-eterna",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Huellas romanas y majestuosidad medieval"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Los escasos yacimientos arqueológicos de Farafra datan predominantemente de la época romana."
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " La región albergó en su día una fortaleza, centinela a lo largo de las antiguas rutas de caravanas."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000021",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " La mayoría de las ruinas romanas se agrupan en torno a Qasr el-Farafra, la actual capital del oasis, que históricamente fue su único pueblo."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000024",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000026",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000025"
              ],
              "text": "El Qasr"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000027",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", una fortaleza que domina el desierto, probablemente se asienta sobre cimientos romanos, ampliados en época medieval con más de 125 habitaciones."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000028",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000029",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " A pesar de "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "00000000002a"
              ],
              "text": "los daños causados por las"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " lluvias de los años 50, sigue siendo un símbolo de resistencia parcialmente habitado. "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000025",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/guia-de-viaje-del-oasis-de-bahariya/pueblo-de-al-qasr/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/bahariya/pueblo-de-al-qasr",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000002a",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/es/el-tiempo-en-egipto/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/es/guide/rosetta-rasheed/el-tiempo-en-rosetta-rashid-y-la-mejor-epoca-para-visitarla",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000002e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Secretos Enterrados y Ermita Cristiana "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000039",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000030",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Cerca de allí hay un antiguo cementerio, donde tumbas excavadas en la roca, algunas "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000032",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000031"
              ],
              "text": "de las"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000033",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " cuales fueron más tarde hogares de antiguos ermitaños cristianos, están casi engullidas por el desierto."
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000034",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "\n"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000035",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Ahmed Fakhry, un venerado arqueólogo egipcio, destacó Ain Besai, a unos 12 km de Qasr el-Farafra, como un yacimiento de importancia, que "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000037",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "cuenta"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000038",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " entre sus tesoros con un cementerio romano y una capilla de piedra caliza. "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000031",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
